1
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:08,360
You have 3 sets of data.

2
00:00:08,410 --> 00:00:13,370
First: your height on every birthday, from age 5 to age 12.

3
00:00:13,420 --> 00:00:16,570
Second: how 30 classmates travel to school.

4
00:00:16,620 --> 00:00:21,070
Third: test scores for boys and girls, in 4 subjects.

5
00:00:21,120 --> 00:00:23,850
Start with your height on every birthday.

6
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:27,500
Is that best shown on a line graph, or on a pie chart?

7
00:00:27,550 --> 00:00:30,730
Pause the video and decide.

8
00:00:30,780 --> 00:00:31,610
A line graph.

9
00:00:31,660 --> 00:00:37,150
Your height changes over time, and a line graph shows that change clearly.

10
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:39,210
Remember the 3 types of data.

11
00:00:39,260 --> 00:00:42,050
Categorical data is words, like colours.

12
00:00:42,100 --> 00:00:45,600
Discrete data is counted, like the number of pets.

13
00:00:45,650 --> 00:00:49,060
Continuous data is measured, like height.

14
00:00:49,110 --> 00:00:51,510
Different charts do different jobs.

15
00:00:51,560 --> 00:00:55,060
A bar chart compares categories, or counts.

16
00:00:55,110 --> 00:00:57,550
A dual bar chart compares 2 groups.

17
00:00:57,600 --> 00:01:00,650
A line graph shows change over time.

18
00:01:00,700 --> 00:01:01,320
Your turn.

19
00:01:01,370 --> 00:01:05,960
Which chart shows the parts of a whole: a pie chart, or a line graph?

20
00:01:06,010 --> 00:01:09,170
Pause the video and decide.

21
00:01:09,220 --> 00:01:09,990
A pie chart.

22
00:01:10,040 --> 00:01:14,320
Each sector is 1 part, and the whole circle is the whole group.

23
00:01:14,370 --> 00:01:17,270
A waffle diagram does the same job.

24
00:01:17,320 --> 00:01:18,980
A good chart has a title.

25
00:01:19,030 --> 00:01:21,780
Its axes have labels, with units.

26
00:01:21,830 --> 00:01:23,960
The scale goes up in equal steps.

27
00:01:24,010 --> 00:01:27,020
For a bar chart, it should start at 0.

28
00:01:27,070 --> 00:01:29,460
If there are colours, there is a key.

29
00:01:29,510 --> 00:01:33,100
And a good chart says where the data came from.

30
00:01:33,150 --> 00:01:34,420
Here is the method.

31
00:01:34,470 --> 00:01:36,630
Step 1: what type of data is it?

32
00:01:36,680 --> 00:01:38,910
Is it measured over time?

33
00:01:38,960 --> 00:01:41,120
Step 2: what do you want to show?

34
00:01:41,170 --> 00:01:44,830
A comparison, the parts of a whole, or a trend?

35
00:01:44,880 --> 00:01:48,680
Step 3: pick the chart, and draw it carefully.

36
00:01:48,730 --> 00:01:52,950
Step 4: add the title, the labels, the units and a key.

37
00:01:53,000 --> 00:02:00,880
A café records the drinks it sells in 1 day: 90 coffees, 45 teas, 30 juices and 15 bottles of water.

38
00:02:00,930 --> 00:02:04,760
Which chart shows the share of each drink?

39
00:02:04,810 --> 00:02:08,570
The shares are parts of a whole, so use a pie chart.

40
00:02:08,620 --> 00:02:13,070
The total is 180 drinks, so each drink gets 2 degrees.

41
00:02:13,120 --> 00:02:19,910
The angles are 180 degrees, 90 degrees, 60 degrees and 30 degrees.

42
00:02:19,960 --> 00:02:25,130
A town records its population every year, from 2015 to 2024.

43
00:02:25,180 --> 00:02:27,940
Which chart should it use?

44
00:02:27,990 --> 00:02:31,420
The data changes over time, so a line graph is best.

45
00:02:31,470 --> 00:02:35,780
It shows the trend: is the population rising, or falling?

46
00:02:35,830 --> 00:02:36,480
Your turn.

47
00:02:36,530 --> 00:02:40,400
You want to compare the scores of 2 classes, in 3 tests.

48
00:02:40,450 --> 00:02:43,480
Do you use a dual bar chart, or a pie chart?

49
00:02:43,530 --> 00:02:46,770
Pause the video and decide.

50
00:02:46,820 --> 00:02:47,960
A dual bar chart.

51
00:02:48,010 --> 00:02:52,570
For each test, draw 2 bars side by side: 1 for each class.

52
00:02:52,620 --> 00:02:54,360
A bar chart has no title.

53
00:02:54,410 --> 00:02:55,940
Its axis starts at 20.

54
00:02:55,990 --> 00:02:57,600
And there are no units.

55
00:02:57,650 --> 00:02:59,800
How can you improve it?

56
00:02:59,850 --> 00:03:00,610
Add a title.

57
00:03:00,660 --> 00:03:05,780
Start the axis at 0, so that the heights of the bars can be compared fairly.

58
00:03:05,830 --> 00:03:08,700
And label the axis, with its units.

59
00:03:08,750 --> 00:03:13,330
A survey of favourite fruit finds: apple 8, banana 5, mango 11.

60
00:03:13,380 --> 00:03:15,670
Here is Ines's plan for a chart.

61
00:03:15,720 --> 00:03:18,280
Which line goes wrong first?

62
00:03:18,330 --> 00:03:19,390
Line 2 is wrong.

63
00:03:19,440 --> 00:03:21,260
Fruit names are categories.

64
00:03:21,310 --> 00:03:27,570
There is nothing in between apple and banana, so joining the points has no meaning.

65
00:03:27,620 --> 00:03:30,230
Use a bar chart for categories.

66
00:03:30,280 --> 00:03:33,210
Be careful with bar charts in adverts.

67
00:03:33,260 --> 00:03:35,960
2 phones score 52 and 55 in a test.

68
00:03:36,010 --> 00:03:41,530
If the axis starts at 50, the bars are 2 units and 5 units tall.

69
00:03:41,580 --> 00:03:45,260
The second bar looks more than 2 times as tall.

70
00:03:45,310 --> 00:03:49,390
But 55 is only about 6 per cent more than 52.

71
00:03:49,440 --> 00:03:52,710
So always look at where the axis starts.

72
00:03:52,760 --> 00:03:53,940
One last question.

73
00:03:53,990 --> 00:04:00,730
The axis of a bar chart should usually start at which number: 0, or the smallest value in the data?

74
00:04:00,780 --> 00:04:03,980
Pause the video and answer.

75
00:04:04,030 --> 00:04:04,320
At 0.

76
00:04:04,370 --> 00:04:09,980
Then the height of each bar matches its value, and the comparison is fair.

77
00:04:10,030 --> 00:04:13,160
To remember: bar charts compare categories.

78
00:04:13,210 --> 00:04:16,150
Dual bar charts compare 2 groups.

79
00:04:16,200 --> 00:04:20,550
Pie charts and waffle diagrams show the parts of a whole.

80
00:04:20,600 --> 00:04:23,450
Line graphs show change over time.

81
00:04:23,500 --> 00:04:27,910
A good chart has a title, labels, units, a key and a fair scale.

82
00:04:27,960 --> 00:04:33,390
Great work! Now practise lesson 16.5 on Camday.
